  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-17:\n\n> bug; simulation is broken; voxel body is not visible at all anymore\n\nWhat happens: in the simulation, the stock body (the voxel body) is not visible.\nExpected: the simulation draws the stock body, and the playback removes material from it.\n\nThe priority is `P2`: this is a regression, and the report names no workaround.\n\n**Not known yet**\n- The build that shows the defect (v0.23.0, or main after it).\n- The project and the operation kinds.\n- If the stock is absent from the start, or only during playback.\n\n**Changes to examine first**\n- PR #2290 \"fix(sim): play the stock up to the first operation with no toolpath\" (merged 2026-11-17, `b7b0de3d5`). It is in main only, not in v0.23.0.\n- #2181, in v0.23.0: the playback calculates the stock removal one time before it plays.\n- #2177, in v0.23.0: stock in a vise and stock turned by a quarter turn.\n\n**First step**\n- Reproduce on main with `examples/` projects, headless where possible and in the windowed program where necessary.\n- Find the first commit that shows the defect.\n\nDone means:\n- The simulation draws the stock body again, at the start and during playback.\n- A test in the default suite asserts that the stock mesh of the simulation is not empty and is drawn. A structural test is sufficient: no pixel snapshot.\n",
